        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f0b94ba0-c9a8-5ed1-8fc1-222d219126c1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ferrari 360, Ferrari F355, Ferrari F430, Porsche 911, Lamborghini Diablo, Mitsubishi Lancer, Subaru Impreza, HSV\n- Organizations: PROCAR\n- Events: 2004 Paris Motor Show\n- Topics: Australian Nations Cup Championship, Australian GT Production Car Championship\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, PROCAR split the Australian GT Production Car Championship into two separate series.\n- In 2000, the new Australian Nations Cup Championship was created for more exotic GT cars such as the Porsche 911, Ferrari 360, and Lamborghini Diablo.\n- In 2000, the revised Australian GT Production Car Championship was intended to let lesser vehicles such as the Mitsubishi Lancer, Subaru Impreza, and HSV compete for outright wins.\n- The Ferrari 360 succeeded the Ferrari F355.\n- The Ferrari F430 replaced the Ferrari 360.\n- The Ferrari F430 debuted at the 2004 Paris Motor Show as the successor to the Ferrari 360.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
